---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const href = (path = '') => `${base}${path}`;
---
<Layout current="docs" title="Documentation — StackPilot">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-kicker">Documentation</div>
      <h1>Build from the golden path.</h1>
      <p>StackPilot is intentionally small at the surface. You choose the service language and deployment profile; StackPilot supplies tested engineering defaults.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="shell docs-layout">
    <aside class="docs-nav">
      <a class="active" href="#quickstart">Quickstart</a>
      <a href="#new">new</a>
      <a href="#plan">plan</a>
      <a href="#bootstrap">bootstrap</a>
      <a href="#doctor">doctor</a>
      <a href="#recipes">recipes</a>
      <a href="#profile">Project profile</a>
    </aside>
    <article class="doc">
      <h2 id="quickstart">Quickstart</h2>
      <p>After <a href={href('install/')}>installing StackPilot</a>, create a production-minded backend service with one command:</p>
      <div class="code-block"><button class="copy-button" data-copy="quick-code">Copy</button><pre id="quick-code"><code>stackpilot new payments-api --language Rust</code></pre></div>
      <p>For Rust, StackPilot resolves <strong>Axum</strong> automatically and applies the default backend profile: PostgreSQL, AWS, Docker, GitHub Actions and Terraform.</p>

      <h2 id="new"><code>stackpilot new</code></h2>
      <p>Creates a new repository directory from a StackPilot recipe. Interactive mode guides you through the small set of decisions that matter.</p>
      <div class="code-block"><pre><code>stackpilot new &lt;project-name&gt;

# Explicit golden path
stackpilot new orders-api --language Go

# Non-interactive automation
stackpilot new orders-api \
  --non-interactive \
  --kind "Backend API" \
  --language Go \
  --framework Auto \
  --database PostgreSQL \
  --cloud AWS \
  --docker true \
  --ci true \
  --terraform true</code></pre></div>

      <h2 id="plan"><code>stackpilot plan</code></h2>
      <p>Preview the files StackPilot intends to generate before it writes anything. This is the recommended path when introducing StackPilot into automation or team workflows.</p>
      <div class="code-block"><button class="copy-button" data-copy="plan-code">Copy</button><pre id="plan-code"><code>stackpilot plan payments-api --language TypeScript</code></pre></div>

      <h2 id="bootstrap"><code>stackpilot bootstrap</code></h2>
      <p>Transforms a repository created with GitHub's <strong>Use this template</strong> button into the selected application foundation in place, then removes StackPilot's template-engine internals.</p>
      <div class="code-block"><button class="copy-button" data-copy="bootstrap-code">Copy</button><pre id="bootstrap-code"><code>stackpilot bootstrap --recipe base</code></pre></div>
      <div class="note">You can also use the <strong>Bootstrap StackPilot</strong> workflow from the repository's GitHub Actions tab instead of running this command locally.</div>

      <h2 id="doctor"><code>stackpilot doctor</code></h2>
      <p>Checks whether the local environment has the basic tools needed for the selected workflow.</p>
      <div class="code-block"><button class="copy-button" data-copy="doctor-code">Copy</button><pre id="doctor-code"><code>stackpilot doctor</code></pre></div>

      <h2 id="recipes"><code>stackpilot recipes</code></h2>
      <p>Lists the recipes available to the StackPilot engine. V0.1 ships around the <code>base</code> recipe, with conditional files implementing the six blessed backend paths.</p>
      <div class="code-block"><button class="copy-button" data-copy="recipes-code">Copy</button><pre id="recipes-code"><code>stackpilot recipes</code></pre></div>

      <h2 id="profile">Project profile</h2>
      <p>Generated repositories include <code>.stackpilot.toml</code>. This records the choices used to generate the repository, giving future StackPilot operations a stable machine-readable description of the project's foundation.</p>
      <div class="code-block"><pre><code>project_name = "payments-api"
kind = "Backend API"
language = "Rust"
framework = "Axum"
database = "PostgreSQL"
cloud = "AWS"
docker = true
ci = true
terraform = true</code></pre></div>

      <h2>What StackPilot does not do yet</h2>
      <p>V0.1 focuses on backend services. Frontend applications, full-stack applications, workers, CLI applications, libraries, repository remediation and hosted organization policies are later phases—not half-supported switches in the first release.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
